Subject: gfx_opengl: framebuffer 0 can be a visionOS eye instead of the window

The visionOS 3D mode renders each eye into an app-owned MTLTexture that ANGLE
draws through an EGLImage-wrapped FBO (app/vision3d/PDEyeTargets.mm, D-048).
This patch is the engine's whole half of that: slot 0 of the backend's
`framebuffers` vector - "the screen" - stops being hard-wired to GL name 0 and
asks pdVisionEyeFBO() instead.

Six paths aim at slot 0 and every one of them follows the redirect unchanged:
the game's direct draw (start_draw_to_framebuffer), the MSAA resolve out of
game_framebuffer, copy_framebuffer, the Vivid Colours / Black Level grade pass,
read_screen_pixels (F12 and --screenshot-frame), and the restore-bind after
each of those. That is why the seam is here and not in gfx_pc: nothing above
the backend learns that a frame is now an eye.

Two latent bugs are fixed on the way, both of which only bite once slot 0 has a
non-zero name:

  * resolve_msaa_color_buffer restored the binding with the framebuffer INDEX
    where the NAME was wanted (`current_framebuffer`, not
    `framebuffers[current_framebuffer].fbo`). The two are the same number only
    while the current slot is 0 and slot 0 is the window.
  * copy_framebuffer and the grade pass asked for GL_BACK as the read buffer of
    slot 0. GL_BACK is legal only for the DEFAULT framebuffer; ES 3.0 raises
    GL_INVALID_OPERATION for the mismatch, which is the same trap patch 0007
    already had to fix once.

Everything is behind TARGET_OS_VISION: on iOS, macOS, Linux and Windows
pd_screen_fbo() is a compile-time `return 0`, the compiler folds every use back
to the literal the code had before, and pdVisionEyeFBO is not referenced at
all. The streaming capture entry points (gfx_opengl_capture_*) still name 0
directly - they are the ffmpeg recorder, which patch 0011 compiles out on iOS
and visionOS entirely.

diff --git a/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp b/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
index 58c2f416f..eac1889d3 100644
--- a/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
+++ b/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
@@ -73,6 +73,48 @@ static uint32_t frame_count;
 
 static std::vector<Framebuffer> framebuffers;
 static size_t current_framebuffer;
+
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// visionOS 3D mode: framebuffer 0 is an EYE, not the window (D-048).
+//
+// Slot 0 of `framebuffers` is "the screen": GL name 0, the window's back
+// buffer. Everything the renderer does at the end of a frame is aimed at it -
+// the game draws straight into it when MSAA is off, the multisampled
+// game_framebuffer is RESOLVED into it when MSAA is on, copy_framebuffer reads
+// it, the Vivid Colours / Black Level grade pass blits out of it and draws back
+// over it, and read_screen_pixels is how F12 and --screenshot-frame get a
+// picture.
+//
+// In the visionOS 3D mode there is no window to present into: each eye is an
+// app-owned MTLTexture wrapped as a real FBO (app/vision3d/PDEyeTargets.mm).
+// Redirecting slot 0 to that FBO is therefore the WHOLE seam - all six paths
+// above follow it for free, and not one line above the backend has to know that
+// a frame is now an eye. The alternative, teaching gfx_pc about eyes, would
+// have put the MSAA resolve, the grade pass and the screenshot on three
+// separate special cases.
+//
+// pdVisionEyeFBO() answers 0 whenever 3D is off, which is the plain window
+// again. On iOS, macOS and every other platform the call does not exist: the
+// helper is a compile-time `return 0` and every use below is the literal the
+// code had before.
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+#include <TargetConditionals.h>
+#endif
+#if defined(TARGET_OS_VISION) && TARGET_OS_VISION
+extern "C" unsigned int pdVisionEyeFBO(int *w, int *h);
+#define PD_VISION_EYE_FB 1
+#else
+#define PD_VISION_EYE_FB 0
+#endif
+
+static inline GLuint pd_screen_fbo(void) {
+#if PD_VISION_EYE_FB
+    return (GLuint)pdVisionEyeFBO(NULL, NULL);
+#else
+    return 0;
+#endif
+}
 static float current_noise_scale;
 static int current_anisotropy_level;
 static FilteringMode current_filter_mode = FILTER_LINEAR;
@@ -2116,14 +2158,15 @@ static void gfx_opengl_grade_frame(void) {
     } else {
         glDisable(GL_SCISSOR_TEST);
 
-        // The window into the texture
-        glBindFramebuffer(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
-        glReadBuffer(GL_BACK);
+        // The window - or, in 3D, the eye - into the texture
+        const GLuint screen_fbo = framebuffers[0].fbo;
+        glBindFramebuffer(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER, screen_fbo);
+        glReadBuffer(screen_fbo ? GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0 : GL_BACK);
         glBindFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, grade_fbo);
         glBlitFramebuffer(0, 0, width, height, 0, 0, width, height, GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT, GL_NEAREST);
 
-        // And back over the window, graded
-        glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
+        // And back over it, graded
+        glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, screen_fbo);
         glDisable(GL_BLEND);
         glDisable(GL_DEPTH_TEST);
         glDisable(GL_CULL_FACE);
@@ -2564,6 +2607,13 @@ static void gfx_opengl_update_framebuffer_parameters(int fb_id, uint32_t width,
                                                      bool can_extract_depth) {
     Framebuffer& fb = framebuffers[fb_id];
 
+    // Slot 0's GL name is not a constant any more (see pd_screen_fbo above):
+    // in 3D it is the eye the engine is about to draw, and the eye rotates
+    // through a ring. Re-read it wherever slot 0 is about to be used.
+    if (fb_id == 0) {
+        fb.fbo = pd_screen_fbo();
+    }
+
     width = max(width, 1U);
     height = max(height, 1U);
 
@@ -2637,6 +2687,9 @@ bool gfx_opengl_start_draw_to_framebuffer(int fb_id, float noise_scale) {
 
     if (gfx_framebuffers_enabled && fb_id < (int)framebuffers.size()) {
         Framebuffer& fb = framebuffers[fb_id];
+        if (fb_id == 0) {
+            fb.fbo = pd_screen_fbo();
+        }
         if (noise_scale != 0.0f) {
             current_noise_scale = 1.0f / noise_scale;
         }
@@ -2682,7 +2735,10 @@ void gfx_opengl_resolve_msaa_color_buffer(int fb_id_target, int fb_id_source) {
     glBindFramebuffer(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER, fb_src.fbo);
     glBlitFramebuffer(0, 0, fb_src.width, fb_src.height, 0, 0, fb_dst.width, fb_dst.height, GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT,
